# Spec and ADR Management

## When to Create

- **Spec:** Before implementing any new feature or significant change that affects behavior visible in:
  - Global requirements (`docs/plans/2026-02-27-task-tracker-requirements.md`)
  - API contracts
  - Data model or plugin interfaces
- **ADR:** When making architecturally significant decisions, such as:
  - Choosing or changing core technologies or patterns.
  - Introducing new integration mechanisms or security models.
  - Adjusting plugin or event architectures.

## Locations

- Feature specs: `docs/specs/NNNN-feature-name/spec.md` (4-digit sequence, kebab-case name).
- ADRs: `docs/adrs/NNNN-decision-name.md` (4-digit sequence, kebab-case name).
- Indexes:
  - `docs/specs/index.md` – lists all specs.
  - `docs/adrs/index.md` – lists all ADRs.

Whenever you add or change a spec/ADR, keep the corresponding index file in sync.

## Spec Format (Minimum)

```markdown
# Spec NNNN: Feature Name

Status: Proposed | In Progress | Completed | Deprecated
Date: YYYY-MM-DD

## Overview

[What and why. Reference relevant FRs from the global requirements doc.]

## Requirements

- [Bullet list of requirements with FR references where applicable]

## Implementation Details

- [Key files changed, major flows, constraints]

## API Changes

- [If any API surface or payloads change, document here]

## Known Limitations

- [Any known gaps, trade-offs, or deferred work]
```

## ADR Format (Minimum)

```markdown
# ADR-NNNN: Title

Status: Proposed | Accepted | Deprecated | Superseded
Date: YYYY-MM-DD

## Context

[What problem are we solving? Why now? What constraints exist?]

## Decision

[What option did we choose? High-level description.]

## Alternatives Considered

- [Alternative 1: pros/cons and why not chosen]
- [Alternative 2: pros/cons and why not chosen]

## Consequences

- Positive: [What becomes easier?]
- Negative: [What becomes harder?]
- Risks: [What risks are introduced?]
```

## Traceability

- Reference FR IDs from `docs/plans/2026-02-27-task-tracker-requirements.md` in specs and tests.
- In ADRs, link to related specs and vice versa.

